        "describe one family member or friend",
        "keep noun and possessive agreement clear"
      ],
      "teaching": {
        "explanation": "French short possessives come before the noun: mon/ma/mes, ton/ta/tes, son/sa/ses, notre/nos. Note that notre does not change for gender (notre ami / notre amie); but French possessives vary by gender and number (and by vowel sound: mon before a feminine noun starting with a vowel).",
        "pattern": "Ma mère est gentille. Notre ami est grand. Sa maison est ici.",
        "note": "Son/sa can mean his or her; context supplies the meaning."
      },
